    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_6">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">6</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description explicitly focuses on 'New materials discovery for HE/Light sources -- New AI/ML,' which directly aligns with the materials-focused Genesis challenge aimed at accelerating discovery and qualification of mission-critical materials using AI. The WBS and STAT context (Dynamic Materials Properties under Assessment Science) further supports that this effort is about material behavior and development for the stockpile, not nonproliferation monitoring or emergency response, making the materials discovery/production challenge the best fit.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">110903334.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_14">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">14</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on AI/ML workflows and frontier-class AI models to reveal causal relationships between material response and expanded underground test (UGT) diagnostic and experimental datasets, under the Assessment Science / Primary Assessment Technologies WBS. This aligns with improving nuclear assessment and response capabilities rather than facility throughput or historical data digitization, matching the mission of accelerating nuclear threat assessment, preparedness, and response. SME correction: Corrected</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">36412500.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_17">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">17</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on using machine learning to predict compatibility and incompatibility of energetic materials, which directly aligns with AI-accelerated materials workflows and qualification for mission-critical materials described in the “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence” challenge. The WBS and STAT context (Aging &amp; Lifetimes, stockpile engineering) further support that this is about materials performance and reliability for the deterrent, not nonproliferation monitoring or digitizing historical data.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">24666363.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_18">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">18</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description is “Materials Aging &amp; Compatibility,” under the Aging &amp; Lifetimes WBS within Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering. This strongly suggests work on understanding and qualifying material behavior over time to ensure reliability of stockpile components. Among the candidate challenges, this aligns best with “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence,” which explicitly targets lifecycle workflows for mission-critical materials and their qualification for deterrence systems. The other challenges focus on nonproliferation monitoring or digitizing historical data, which do not match the materials aging and compatibility focus. Confidence is medium because the description is brief and does not explicitly mention AI workflows, but the materials and qualification context fits this challenge most closely.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">29440823.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_22">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">22</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on characterizing and validating energetic and shock mitigation materials to increase the credibility of computational models, and on curating and analyzing flight test data to predict environments of future systems. This directly aligns with AI-accelerated materials workflows and model-based qualification for strategic components described in the materials discovery and qualification challenge, rather than archival data digitization or nonproliferation monitoring. The WBS and STAT context (Stockpile Research, Engineering, Delivery Environments) further support a stockpile materials and qualification mission focus.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">22175000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_30">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">30</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on applying AI/ML techniques for qualification of CT data for part acceptance, which directly aligns with AI-accelerated qualification and certification workflows for materials and components. The associated WBS and STAT levels emphasize Advanced Certification &amp; Qualification, matching the challenge centered on accelerating materials discovery, production, and especially qualification for strategic deterrence, rather than broader design/production integration or historic data digitization.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">1750000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_31">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">31</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on automated defect detection and machine learning models for additively manufactured (AM) metal components, which directly supports improving manufacturing reliability and qualification of critical materials and parts. The associated WBS and STAT lines emphasize advanced manufacturing development and weapon technology and manufacturing maturation, aligning with the challenge centered on AI-driven workflows for materials production and qualification rather than enterprise-wide design/production integration or facility experimental throughput.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">5750000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_32">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">32</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on developing a large language model to identify replacement HE binder candidates and on developing high‑performance, multimetal alloys optimized for strength and stability with new additive manufacturing methods that meet future system requirements. This is directly about discovering and developing new materials and qualifying them for future systems, aligned with advanced manufacturing. That maps most closely to the materials-focused challenge on accelerating materials discovery, production, and qualification, rather than enterprise-wide design/production integration or experimental facility throughput.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">11537446.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:harnessing_america_s_historic_nuclear_data_and_r:6cbae10ba9" id="leads_challenge">
      <data key="d11">leads_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">ProgramOffice_Mapping.csv</data>
      <data key="d14">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:harnessing_america_s_historic_nuclear_data_and_r:6cbae10ba9" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_19">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">19</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on AI/ML tools to automatically index, catalog, extract metadata, and enable search across an increased number of digital repositories. This aligns directly with the challenge to digitize, structure, and make accessible historic nuclear data and records via AI-driven digitization and information extraction pipelines, rather than materials development or production-process optimization.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">77548915.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:harnessing_america_s_historic_nuclear_data_and_r:6cbae10ba9" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_21">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">21</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on expanding deployment of a tool suite to perform data conditioning, curation, and labeling for legacy weapons data across design agencies. This aligns directly with the challenge centered on digitizing, organizing, and making historic nuclear and weapons data usable for research and AI, rather than on integrating design/production workflows or accelerating materials development. The WBS category of Archiving &amp; Support further supports a data- and archive-focused mission, matching the historic data challenge.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">153848000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="leads_challenge">
      <data key="d11">leads_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">ProgramOffice_Mapping.csv</data>
      <data key="d14">3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_3">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">3</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on productionizing AI tools for weapons design, modeling, simulation workflows, and meshing (e.g., CHANDLER federated model, Horizon Shield workflow, CADSAT meshing), plus deploying GPUs, cloud access, optimized storage, and a Secure AI suite on classified networks. This aligns most closely with the data- and workflow-centric nature of the “Harnessing America’s Historic Nuclear Data and Research” challenge, which emphasizes AI pipelines, digitization, meshing, simulation-ready datasets, secure archives, and cross-classification access controls. While there is some overlap with design/production integration and experimental capacity, the emphasis here is on AI infrastructure and tools that turn information into secure, simulation-ready assets rather than on DA/PA production integration or facility operations, so the historic data/research challenge is the best fit given the available evidence. SME correction: Corrected</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">346644000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_4">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
