    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:5" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_5">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">5</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on productionizing AI tools for weapons design, modeling, and simulation workflows (e.g., CHANDLER federated model, Horizon Shield simulation workflow, CADSAT meshing tool) and deploying supporting infrastructure (GPUs, cloud, optimized storage) plus a Secure AI suite on classified networks. This aligns most closely with the data- and workflow-centric nature of the “Harnessing America’s Historic Nuclear Data and Research” challenge, which emphasizes AI pipelines, meshing, simulation-ready datasets, secure archives, and cross-classification access controls. While there is some overlap with design/production integration and experimental capacity, the emphasis here is on AI-enabled modeling/simulation and secure data/compute infrastructure rather than DA/PA production integration or facility operations, so the historic data and research challenge is the best fit. SME correction: Corrected</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">338521000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
