    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:12" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_12">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">12</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes NA-11’s UFR titled “Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence,” and the WBS/STAT context is Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering with Dynamic Materials Properties—both tightly coupled to weapons design, certification, and production activities. Among the candidate challenges, the one explicitly focused on nuclear deterrence and integrating AI into design/production operations is “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence,” making it the best fit. The other two challenges focus on business/management processes and acquisition, which are not indicated in the scope text. Confidence is medium because the description is high-level and references the overall Genesis Mission rather than a specific MiSTC by name.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">9127000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
