    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:15" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_15">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">15</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI/ML work across multiple high-energy-density (HED) experiments, focusing on analysis and modeling of experimental data to develop more refined approaches. This aligns most closely with the challenge centered on increasing experimental capacity at nuclear research facilities, which targets AI-driven optimization of experiments, data fusion, and improved throughput at limited-capacity, high-consequence facilities. The other challenges focus on historical data digitization or design/production integration rather than ongoing experimental campaign analysis and optimization.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">44130500.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
