    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:16" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_16">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">16</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">Scope centers on NA-11’s AI tools for nuclear deterrence within Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering / Assessment Science / Secondary Assessment Technologies, which aligns most directly with AI applied to weapons design, assessment, and production operations rather than business management or acquisition workflows. The prior UFR title “Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence” and the technical WBS context support mapping to the design/production-focused Genesis Mission challenge, even though the scope text is high-level and references both platform and MiSTC objectives, lowering confidence slightly.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">56442000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
