      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes that the decrement primarily affects workforce (17 FTEs) and AI/ML tools across laboratories, plants, and sites, while noting that critical AI/ML endeavors remain a strategic priority. This points to AI being used to support cross-cutting activities and processes rather than a specific materials R&amp;D pipeline or facility safety-basis automation. The WBS and STAT hierarchy (Archiving &amp; Support under Engineering) and the A&amp;S (Assessment &amp; Support) decrement context suggest business/management and support functions. Among the options, this aligns best with the challenge focused on accelerating business and management processes for national security missions, which targets enterprise-wide AI-enabled efficiencies in planning, programming, and support workflows rather than materials discovery or detailed regulatory/safety process streamlining in production facilities.</data>
      <data key="d18">DECREMENT</data>
      <data key="d19">-10365000.0</data>
