    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:25" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_25">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">25</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description explicitly references the NA-11 UFR titled “Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence,” which aligns most directly with the design/production-focused nuclear deterrence challenge rather than business management or acquisition. The WBS/STAT context (Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering; Inertial Confinement Fusion; Facility Operations) also points toward core weapons R&amp;D and production operations, consistent with integrating AI into nuclear deterrence design and production workflows, not primarily into business processes or acquisition systems. While the description is high-level Genesis-wide AI, the explicit nuclear deterrence framing makes the design/production challenge the best fit.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">33690000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
