      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes NA-11’s UFR titled “Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence,” tied to stockpile-related HED &amp; Ignition Science, indicating AI capabilities focused on nuclear deterrence design and production missions rather than business processes or acquisition. Among the Genesis Mission challenges, this aligns most directly with “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence,” which targets AI-enabled design/production integration for nuclear deterrence. The other two challenges focus on enterprise business/management workflows and acquisition systems, which are not mentioned in the scope text.</data>
