    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:37" target="mstc_challenge:safeguarding_nuclear_materials_from_proliferatio:616a01e1a8" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_37">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">37</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on accelerating AI for challenging proliferation detection scenarios, including AI-driven process modeling and AI-enabled system-of-systems digital twins, directly aligned with nonproliferation monitoring and detection. The STAT lines are Proliferation Detection under Defense Nuclear Nonproliferation R&amp;D, and the program request is explicitly “AI ACCELERATION FOR DETECTION OF FOREIGN PROLIFERATION.” This matches the Safeguarding Nuclear Materials from Proliferation Threats challenge, which centers on AI-enabled detection of proliferation activities, rather than digitization of historical data or AI-induced proliferation risks.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">342000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA20</data>
    </edge>
