    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:38" target="mstc_challenge:streamlining_production_removing_red_tape_and_en:5c22e0a6a3" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_38">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">38</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on automation and AI/ML to enhance the e810 system and streamline the process for submitting civil nuclear technology transfer requests under 10 CFR Part 810. This is fundamentally an acquisition/authorization workflow and process-efficiency problem—improving how requests are submitted, processed, and managed—rather than directly detecting proliferation anomalies or digitizing historic nuclear data. Among the options, it best aligns with the acquisition-focused challenge that aims to apply AI to streamline complex, regulation-driven federal processes, even though this specific case is export/technology transfer rather than procurement. The nonproliferation context (NA-20, civil nuclear cooperation) supports the mission area but the primary activity is process streamlining, matching “Accelerating Nuclear Enterprise Acquisition” more closely than the other two challenges. SME correction: Corrected</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">17500000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA20</data>
    </edge>
