    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:40" target="mstc_challenge:safeguarding_nuclear_materials_from_proliferatio:616a01e1a8" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_40">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">40</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on export control IT upgrades to accelerate statutory technical reviews of export licenses for U.S. nuclear and dual-use commodities. This directly supports nonproliferation and control of nuclear-related exports, aligning with NA-20 and STAT/WBS labels such as Nonproliferation and Arms Control and Nuclear Export Controls. Among the options, this most closely matches the Safeguarding Nuclear Materials from Proliferation Threats challenge, which centers on preventing proliferation through improved monitoring, analysis, and control of nuclear materials and related activities, rather than enterprise acquisition processes or weapons design/production integration.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">8000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA20</data>
    </edge>
