    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:41" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_41">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">41</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on designing and maintaining major reactor plant components and systems for technologically superior naval nuclear propulsion, which aligns most closely with integrating advanced design and production capabilities for nuclear-related systems. Among the options, the “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence” challenge is centered on AI-enabled, model-based engineering and production integration for nuclear weapons and related systems, making it the best fit. The other challenges emphasize acquisition process optimization or AI-induced proliferation prevention, which are less directly related to reactor systems design and production. Confidence is medium because the description is naval propulsion–specific rather than explicitly deterrence-focused, but it still best matches the design/production integration theme.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">16200000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA30</data>
    </edge>
