    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:45" target="mstc_challenge:cui_preventing_ai_induced_nuclear_proliferation:bbeffc2cf1" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_45">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">45</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes advancing AI tools for rapid and effective response to nuclear and radiological events, detailed analysis of vast and varied data, and nuclear risk mitigation and response. These align directly with the challenge focused on shrinking detection-to-response times via a continuously learning, multimodal AI fusion system for real-time decision support in nuclear/radiological events. While the description also mentions improving nuclear forensics, the dominant focus is on event response and situational awareness rather than primary attribution, making the ‘Accelerating Nuclear Threat Assessment, Preparedness, and Response’ challenge the best fit. SME correction: Corrected</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">40000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA80</data>
    </edge>
