    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na90:e748b0fc5d" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_49">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">49</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on upgrading electrical power capacity at LANL, including new distribution lines to the Supercomputing Center and between substations. This directly supports increased power and reliability for high-performance computing and experimental facilities, which aligns most closely with expanding experimental and computational throughput at nuclear research sites. While not materials- or acquisition-focused, it is clearly mission-enabling infrastructure for experiments and simulations, fitting best under Increasing Experimental Capacity at Nuclear Research Facilities.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">115104000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA90</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na90:e748b0fc5d" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_50">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">50</data>
      <data key="d15">low</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope describes constructing a new central computing facility to ensure reliable classified and unclassified computing availability, providing space for network and data servers/hubs and personnel. This is a general-purpose computing and data infrastructure project rather than a materials workflow or design/production integration effort. Among the options, it most plausibly supports the data-centric, archival, and AI-accessible infrastructure envisioned in “Harnessing America’s Historic Nuclear Data and Research,” which depends on secure, scalable computing and data environments. However, the description is high-level and not explicitly tied to digitization or historical data, so confidence is low. SME correction: Corrected</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">183700000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA90</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na90:e748b0fc5d" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_52">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">52</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on an Electrical Power Capacity Upgrade at LANL, which most directly supports increasing facility capacity and reliability. Among the options, this aligns best with “Increasing Experimental Capacity at Nuclear Research Facilities,” as enhanced electrical power infrastructure is a prerequisite for higher experimental throughput and more robust operations at nuclear research sites. The other two challenges center on acquisition process optimization and enterprise business/management platforms, which are less directly related to physical infrastructure upgrades.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">2824000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA90</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na90:e748b0fc5d" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_53">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">53</data>
      <data key="d15">low</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description indicates funding for a “New Central Computing Facility, Y-12 OPCs,” which most directly relates to building or upgrading computing and facility infrastructure. Among the options, this aligns best with “Increasing Experimental Capacity at Nuclear Research Facilities,” since enhanced central computing at a nuclear site would support higher experimental throughput and facility operations. There is no explicit link to materials workflows or acquisition modernization, so the mapping is inferred from the facility/computing context, resulting in low confidence.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">3399000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA90</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na90:e748b0fc5d" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_business_and_management_processes_f:1739dbeef6" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_51">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">51</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes “Telecommunication &amp; AI Infrastructure Program Integration” under an AI GENESIS PLATFORM with an OPS AND MAINTENANCE request, indicating enterprise-level AI/IT platform and infrastructure support rather than direct experimental facility operations or materials R&amp;D. This aligns best with the business and management challenge, which focuses on unified platforms and AI-enabled workflows to support planning, operations, and management processes across the enterprise. The WBS and STAT categories (Infrastructure and Operations / Operations of Facilities) further suggest enabling infrastructure for broader mission support, consistent with accelerating business and management processes rather than experimental capacity or materials qualification.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">15220000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA90</data>
    </edge>
