    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:60" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_60">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">60</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope describes a mixed-classification high-performance computing resource to support NNSA’s growing mission demand, with emphasis on efficient use of HPC across classifications. Among the options, this aligns best with the nuclear threat assessment challenge, which explicitly calls out leveraging NNSA’s HPC resources and cross-classification data governance for mission-critical, physics-informed AI in nuclear emergency and threat-response contexts. The other two challenges focus on business/management workflows or design–production integration for deterrence rather than a generalized mixed-classification HPC platform. Because the description is generic and references an NA-114 whitepaper for details, confidence is medium rather than high. SME correction: Corrected</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">45000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NAIM</data>
