    <edge source="sub_office:na20:3f63a5531c" target="mstc_challenge:safeguarding_nuclear_materials_from_proliferatio:616a01e1a8" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_36">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">36</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description is generic (“AI PROGRAM WORK”), so supporting fields drive the mapping. The STAT hierarchy is Defense Nuclear Nonproliferation R&amp;D with a focus on Proliferation Detection, directly aligning with AI-enabled monitoring and detection of nuclear proliferation activities. Among the candidate challenges, “Safeguarding Nuclear Materials from Proliferation Threats” explicitly targets nonproliferation and detection of proliferation-relevant anomalies, matching the Proliferation Detection WBS/STAT context, whereas the other options focus on AI-induced proliferation risk or materials discovery for deterrence rather than nonproliferation R&amp;D.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">165000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA20</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na20:3f63a5531c" target="mstc_challenge:safeguarding_nuclear_materials_from_proliferatio:616a01e1a8" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_37">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">37</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on accelerating AI for challenging proliferation detection scenarios, including AI-driven process modeling and AI-enabled system-of-systems digital twins, directly aligned with nonproliferation monitoring and detection. The STAT lines are Proliferation Detection under Defense Nuclear Nonproliferation R&amp;D, and the program request is explicitly “AI ACCELERATION FOR DETECTION OF FOREIGN PROLIFERATION.” This matches the Safeguarding Nuclear Materials from Proliferation Threats challenge, which centers on AI-enabled detection of proliferation activities, rather than digitization of historical data or AI-induced proliferation risks.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">342000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA20</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na20:3f63a5531c" target="mstc_challenge:safeguarding_nuclear_materials_from_proliferatio:616a01e1a8" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_39">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">39</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on supporting and implementing activities under an Executive Order and expanding IAEA safeguards at U.S. nuclear facilities, which is directly tied to international safeguards, verification, and nonproliferation. The WBS and STAT hierarchy (Nonproliferation and Arms Control; Civil Nuclear Cooperation &amp; Engagement) and NA-20 context further align with global nonproliferation monitoring and safeguarding nuclear materials, matching the Safeguarding Nuclear Materials from Proliferation Threats challenge more closely than experimental capacity or acquisition-focused challenges.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">20000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA20</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na20:3f63a5531c" target="mstc_challenge:safeguarding_nuclear_materials_from_proliferatio:616a01e1a8" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_40">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">40</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on export control IT upgrades to accelerate statutory technical reviews of export licenses for U.S. nuclear and dual-use commodities. This directly supports nonproliferation and control of nuclear-related exports, aligning with NA-20 and STAT/WBS labels such as Nonproliferation and Arms Control and Nuclear Export Controls. Among the options, this most closely matches the Safeguarding Nuclear Materials from Proliferation Threats challenge, which centers on preventing proliferation through improved monitoring, analysis, and control of nuclear materials and related activities, rather than enterprise acquisition processes or weapons design/production integration.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">8000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA20</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na20:3f63a5531c" target="mstc_challenge:strengthening_deterrence_through_attribution_of:12318fe125" id="partners_on_challenge">
      <data key="d11">partners_on_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">ProgramOffice_Mapping.csv</data>
      <data key="d14">7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na20:3f63a5531c" target="mstc_challenge:strengthening_deterrence_through_attribution_of:12318fe125" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_35">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">35</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description explicitly focuses on accelerating nuclear forensics attribution timelines for nuclear or radiological incidents and leveraging AI for post-event processing. This directly aligns with the attribution and nuclear forensics emphasis of the “Strengthening Deterrence Through Attribution of Nuclear and Radiological Signatures” challenge, rather than enterprise acquisition or broader threat assessment/preparedness. Supporting evidence includes the STAT lines for Forensics R&amp;D and the program request title “AI ACCELERATION FOR NUCLEAR FORENSICS TIMELINES.”</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">150000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA20</data>
    </edge>
