      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes “rapid and effective response to nuclear and radiological events” and “detailed analysis of vast and varied data,” which directly mirrors the problem statement and proposed solution language of the Accelerating Nuclear Threat Assessment, Preparedness, and Response challenge. While the scope also mentions improving the speed and accuracy of nuclear forensics analyses (which relates to attribution), the primary framing is event response and risk mitigation, and the program request explicitly references “NUCLEAR RISK MITIGATION AND RESPONSE.” Therefore the dominant alignment is with the threat assessment, preparedness, and response challenge rather than the attribution-focused challenge. SME correction: Corrected</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">17500000.0</data>
